WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.213
The clicking, typing, and copying you still do by hand.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:14.200
RPA promised to take it off you. But every robot was built by hand, and fixed by hand whenever a screen changed.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.606
Now AI builds it.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.486
Describe the job, and Kitewell lays out every step for you to check.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.200
Or build it from Claude Code or Codex, over MCP.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.832
On the first run, AI learns the job in your browser.

00:00:29.832 --> 00:00:32.800
Then your computer runs it, every day.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:37.550
When a site changes, AI finds the new way, and keeps it.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.950
It stops for your OK where it matters.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.900
Got a list in Excel? It runs every row and writes the results back.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:51.914
Coding agents too. Claude Code writes the fix, Codex reviews it, and nothing ships until you approve.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.800
It runs on your computer, and your passwords stay there.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:59.900
Run it on every computer, and watch them all from the cloud.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.034
If a run fails, or a computer goes quiet, you hear about it.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.410
Kitewell.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.400
It flies on its own.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.336
You hold the string.
